WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.130
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Grammar, level A one.

2
00:00:05.430 --> 00:00:08.723
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.023 --> 00:00:15.414
Unit thirty-nine: Review: A1 Grammar. Today you will review everything you learned in A1 Grammar.

4
00:00:15.714 --> 00:00:18.331
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:19.267 --> 00:00:22.708
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:23.550 --> 00:00:24.551
Am / is / are.

7
00:00:25.550 --> 00:00:28.153
Am / is / are means the present forms of the verb be.

8
00:00:28.750 --> 00:00:30.274
I am, she is, they are.

9
00:00:30.883 --> 00:00:33.547
Your turn. Say: Am / is / are.

10
00:00:36.400 --> 00:00:37.413
Am / is / are.

11
00:00:38.150 --> 00:00:39.383
Present simple.

12
00:00:40.383 --> 00:00:43.451
Present simple means the tense for habits and routines.

13
00:00:44.050 --> 00:00:45.806
I play football every day.

14
00:00:46.417 --> 00:00:49.359
Your turn. Say: Present simple.

15
00:00:52.200 --> 00:00:53.259
Present simple.

16
00:00:54.017 --> 00:00:54.809
Can.

17
00:00:55.817 --> 00:00:57.723
Can means the word for ability.

18
00:00:58.317 --> 00:00:59.515
I can swim.

19
00:01:00.117 --> 00:01:02.467
Your turn. Say: Can.

20
00:01:05.333 --> 00:01:05.998
Can.

21
00:01:06.750 --> 00:01:07.739
There is.

22
00:01:08.750 --> 00:01:11.945
There is means the phrase to say that something exists.

23
00:01:12.550 --> 00:01:14.213
There is a cat in the garden.

24
00:01:14.817 --> 00:01:17.875
Your turn. Say: There is.

25
00:01:20.733 --> 00:01:21.897
There is.

26
00:01:22.650 --> 00:01:23.500
Question.

27
00:01:24.517 --> 00:01:27.573
Question means a sentence that asks for information.

28
00:01:28.183 --> 00:01:29.347
Do you like tea?

29
00:01:29.950 --> 00:01:32.393
Your turn. Say: Question.

30
00:01:35.233 --> 00:01:36.014
Question.

31
00:01:36.750 --> 00:01:37.693
Negative.

32
00:01:38.683 --> 00:01:41.182
Negative means saying that something is not true.

33
00:01:41.783 --> 00:01:43.191
I don't like coffee.

34
00:01:43.783 --> 00:01:46.668
Your turn. Say: Negative.

35
00:01:49.533 --> 00:01:50.383
Negative.

36
00:01:51.150 --> 00:01:52.012
Plural.

37
00:01:53.017 --> 00:01:54.447
Plural means more than one.

38
00:01:55.050 --> 00:01:56.678
Boxes is a plural noun.

39
00:01:57.283 --> 00:01:59.866
Your turn. Say: Plural.

40
00:02:02.700 --> 00:02:03.655
Plural.

41
00:02:04.417 --> 00:02:05.406
Sentence.

42
00:02:06.417 --> 00:02:09.577
Sentence means a group of words with a subject and a verb.

43
00:02:10.183 --> 00:02:11.695
This is a sentence.

44
00:02:12.283 --> 00:02:14.982
Your turn. Say: Sentence.

45
00:02:17.833 --> 00:02:18.892
Sentence.

46
00:02:19.700 --> 00:02:23.699
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:24.550 --> 00:02:28.352
Visal, this is the last lesson of A1. What can you remember?

48
00:02:29.450 --> 00:02:38.084
I can make sentences with am, is and are. I know the present simple, can, and there is. I can also ask questions and make negatives.

49
00:02:39.183 --> 00:02:41.833
Which new grammar did we learn in the second half?

50
00:02:42.917 --> 00:02:55.705
The present continuous, was and were, the past simple, comparatives, superlatives, going to, and polite requests. We also learned adverbs and many prepositions.

51
00:02:56.817 --> 00:02:58.410
How can you keep improving?

52
00:02:59.517 --> 00:03:10.902
Read a little, speak every day, and write short sentences. Check your verb forms, your plural nouns and your question words. Small habits make strong grammar.

53
00:03:12.067 --> 00:03:13.695
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:14.550 --> 00:03:17.525
Grammar focus: A1 grammar review.

55
00:03:17.825 --> 00:03:19.035
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:19.750 --> 00:03:20.890
She is a student.

57
00:03:21.783 --> 00:03:23.179
I don't like coffee.

58
00:03:24.083 --> 00:03:25.990
There are two boxes on the table.

59
00:03:26.933 --> 00:03:34.172
Check the subject, the verb form and the word order. Remember am / is / are, the present simple, can, there is, questions, negatives and plurals.

60
00:03:34.917 --> 00:03:38.126
Be careful! Don't say: They is at school.

61
00:03:40.067 --> 00:03:41.962
Say: They are at school.

62
00:03:42.262 --> 00:03:43.414
Use are with they.

63
00:03:44.200 --> 00:03:46.620
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:03:47.433 --> 00:03:48.527
Looking Back.

65
00:03:48.827 --> 00:03:52.336
In A1 we learned am, is and are, and the present simple.

66
00:03:53.333 --> 00:03:55.809
We can make a question and a negative sentence.

67
00:03:56.800 --> 00:03:59.194
We can use can, there is and there are.

68
00:04:00.200 --> 00:04:03.094
We know plural nouns and we can build a full sentence.

69
00:04:04.100 --> 00:04:07.876
With practice, our English grows stronger every day.

70
00:04:08.967 --> 00:04:12.864
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:13.717 --> 00:04:15.031
She blank a student.

72
00:04:15.331 --> 00:04:18.369
A, am. B, is. C, are.

73
00:04:21.933 --> 00:04:23.561
The answer is B: is.

74
00:04:24.717 --> 00:04:27.183
I blank like coffee. (negative)

75
00:04:27.483 --> 00:04:30.556
A, don't. B, doesn't. C, isn't.

76
00:04:34.100 --> 00:04:35.763
The answer is A: don't.

77
00:04:36.917 --> 00:04:39.314
blank you play football? (question)

78
00:04:39.614 --> 00:04:42.895
A, Does. B, Do. C, Are.

79
00:04:46.433 --> 00:04:48.073
The answer is B: Do.

80
00:04:49.217 --> 00:04:50.833
Which sentence is correct?

81
00:04:51.133 --> 00:04:56.679
A, There is two boxes.. B, There are two boxes.. C, There be two boxes..

82
00:05:00.233 --> 00:05:03.034
The answer is B: There are two boxes..

83
00:05:04.183 --> 00:05:07.472
According to the reading, how does English grow stronger?

84
00:05:07.772 --> 00:05:12.365
A, with practice. B, with a long break. C, with silence.

85
00:05:15.900 --> 00:05:17.853
The answer is A: with practice.

86
00:05:19.067 --> 00:05:22.125
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:05:22.983 --> 00:05:25.633
Which A1 grammar point is easiest for you now?

88
00:05:34.417 --> 00:05:35.871
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:05:36.171 --> 00:05:50.668
I think the easiest grammar point for me is am, is and are. I use it every day to talk about myself and my family. Now I also feel more confident with questions, negatives and plural nouns, and I want to keep practising.

90
00:05:50.968 --> 00:05:52.665
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:05:53.550 --> 00:05:57.851
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and a1 grammar review.

92
00:05:58.151 --> 00:06:03.697
Today's value is growth mindset. Mistakes help you grow. Keep learning, step by step.

93
00:06:03.997 --> 00:06:10.390
Congratulations! You have finished Online Grammar, level A one. See you in Online Grammar, level A two!

94
00:06:10.690 --> 00:06:13.528
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

